s of Man explores the essential elements and teachings of the world's predominant faiths, including Hinduism, Buddhism, Confucianism, Taoism, Islam, Judaism, Christianity, and the native traditions of the Americas, Australia, Africa, and Oceania. The author emphasizes the inner, rather than institutional, dimensions of these religions and gives special attention to Zen, Tibetan Buddhism, Sufism, and the teachings of Jesus. He conveys the unique appeal and gifts of each of the traditions and reveals their hold on the human heart and imagination."},"latest_revision":36,"revision":36,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-05-18T14:05:31.008808"}}},"ISBN:9780060571108":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780060571108","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL24262714M/The_World's_Religions_Revised_and_Updated","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL24262714M/The_World's_Religions_Revised_and_Updated","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6411113-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["HarperCollins"],"physical_format":"Electronic resource","source_records":["marc_overdrive/InternetArchiveCrMarc-2010-06-11k.mrc:6815920:2537","bwb:9780061763489","bwb:9780060571108"],"title":"The World's Religions, Revised and Updated","identifiers":{"overdrive":["4DAF1C97-BDF3-4D12-A8F9-9129442613ED"]},"isbn_13":["9780060571108","9780061763489","9780060769543"],"covers":[6411113],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"publish_date":"2003","publish_country":"nyu","key":"/books/OL24262714M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL716209A","name":"Huston Smith"}],"publish_places":["New York"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3930654W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["BL80.2.S645 2003"],"latest_revision":7,"revision":7,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2010-06-17T21:13:44.897879"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-12-17T03:05:38.823321"}}},"ISBN:9780